@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] lilly-durable-receipt-is-not-lifecycle-authority
The local command store is a durable delivery cache of Marshall intent. Neither receipt
success, transport timeout nor connection loss establishes physical stop, frees
allocations, or authorizes a new recovery generation (ADR-0013, ADR-0016).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] lilly-operator-owned-execution-paths
Runtime, credential, image and executable paths MUST originate from validated local
operator configuration or be derived from validated identities; a remote VM command
must never choose a local path (ADR-0017, ADR-0021).
